* PWD - DISPLAY NAMED DIRECTORIES

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* PWD - DISPLAY NAMED DIRECTORIES

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:PWD [name-patterns | drives: | ~drives: | /options]

Displays the Z-System named-directory table. Name patterns are
automatically expanded for matching. Without arguments, displays the
configured entries.

The /P option can include directory passwords when wheel access permits
it. Do not use that option in caller-visible output or shared logs. PWD is
private here even though ordinary listing is read-only.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
